<<<
sustain. Mr » Master of the

Hounds, has sustained a broken rib & other injuries through his horse falling.
===
**sustain.** *Mr ——, Master of the —— Hounds, has sustained a broken rib & other injuries through his horse falling.*
>>>

<<<
but with such abstract objects as injury, loss, leak, bruise, &c., instead of broken rib it is as old as the 15th c., & the extension is not a violent one.
===
but with such abstract objects as *injury, loss, leak, bruise,* &c., instead of *broken rib* it is as old as the 15th c., & the extension is not a violent one.
>>>

<<<
Nevertheless, sustain as a synonym for suffer or receive or get belongs to the class of FORMAL WORDS, & is better avoided both for that reason & for a stronger one:
===
Nevertheless, *sustain* as a synonym for *suffer* or *receive* or *get* belongs to the class of ^^FORMAL WORDS^^, & is better avoided both for that reason & for a stronger one:
>>>

